mption / coverage) against real line numbers.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.0562,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:118-120 — the handler returns JSONResponse({\"in_flight\": gauge.value}) and nothing else.' — but _mcp_health.py:112-156 is store_status() which already returns {path, present, expected}; lines 118-120 are inside its docstring.","Plan: 'infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:130 — the blue-green readiness gate promotes on that same probe.' — autodeploy.sh:130 is `MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=\"${MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT:-120}\"`, a config default, not the gate.","Plan: 'src/rebar/mcp_server.py:759-761 — the boot sweep is guarded by if os.path.isdir(_tracker) ... comment at :752 ... debug line at :769'. Actual :759-761 is compose_startup_opcert_binding; the boot sweep is at :748-750 (run_startup_store_sweep); the isdir guard lives in _mcp_health.py:180 using variable `tracker`, not `_tracker`.","search_files for `os.path.isdir(_tracker)` returned no matches.","run_startup_store_sweep() at _mcp_health.py:159 already emits the no-store branch (line 180: `if os.path.isdir(tracker)` … else log-and-continue)."],"finding":"The plan's Evidence line/symbol citations do not resolve to the code they describe in the current repo; the fix they presuppose as absent is already substantially implemented.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59aefce66fae9d39","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Evidence section (all four bullets)","norm_id":"nf2cf2b4ff6a1cafa","priority":0.7438,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer opens the cited lines to make the change and finds unrelated code (opcert binding, a timeout default, a docstring), or finds the fix already present."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Repoint the boot-sweep evidence to _mcp_health.run_startup_store_sweep() (src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:159-185, isdir guard at :180 on variable `tracker`) and the boot call site at mcp_server.py:748-750; repoint the gate evidence to the actual autodeploy readiness-probe line rather than :130; and note that store_status() at _mcp_health.py:112-156 already satisfies AC-1's '/health reports store status', narrowing this ticket to the gate-consumption and storeless-container coverage ACs.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for the approach and make the 'expected' distinction load-bearing in the body (not just parenthetically): the readiness gate must trip ONLY when a store is expected AND absent, so a legitimately-storeless deployment is not marked unhealthy; note that boot deliberately stays log-and-continue (a missing store must not abort boot) and the observability comes from the store-status field, not from failing.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6743,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'either /health reports store status, or a separate readiness endpoint does and the autodeploy gate consumes it' — states WHAT but not the report-don't-fail rationale.","AC3: 'Coverage asserts a storeless container does not pass the readiness gate (when a store is expected)' — the crucial 'when expected' qualifier appears only parenthetically with no rationale.","'Why this matters' explains why the PROBLEM matters but gives no positive rationale for why THIS approach (report status + gate on expected-AND-absent) is the fit.","The mechanism only works correctly if the gate keys on 'expected AND not present'; gating on 'not present' alone is a plausible naive misreading that would regress legitimately-storeless deploys."],"finding":"The plan does not state a positive rationale for its chosen approach, and in particular under-specifies the load-bearing 'expected' distinction — that the readiness gate must trip only when a store is EXPECTED but ABSENT, never on absence alone. AC1/AC3 gesture at this with 'when a store is expected' but the plan never explains WHY (a deployment that never configured a tracker legitimately has no store, so gating on presence alone would refuse to promote a good container and take the endpoint down to report a non-problem).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcb68c1a6705129e4","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC1, AC3) and 'Why this matters'","norm_id":"neac0f8bc79ec9d66","priority":0.1257,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer gates the readiness signal on store presence alone; a dev/unprovisioned deployment that never configured a tracker dir is now refused promotion and its endpoint taken down to report a non-problem.","A reviewer of the resulting change cannot tell whether hard-fail-on-absent vs report-degraded was a considered decision."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a short rationale paragraph: define how 'expected' is determined (deferred to the sibling provisioning ticket / a tracker-dir override) and state that the gate keys on 'expected AND not present' precisely so the change is inert on legitimately-storeless boxes and becomes strict only once a store is configured — no flag day, and boot remains log-and-continue rather than fail-closed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"7d7c6558d26da027","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["06563ab4758944cb",2095],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["129cf9bd4d7b9514",7],"ticket_id":["59039edcc8f15b8a",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":6016.1,"input_tokens":342994,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":287771.6,"output_tokens":24115,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":307710.5,"verify_requests":7},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structu